WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.990 --> 00:00:06.990
Data centers are the backbone of our
digital world.

2
00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:11.990
Every click, every AI model, every video
stream depends on them.

3
00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:15.990
But as workloads grow, so does the heat
they generate.

4
00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:20.990
Traditional air cooling methods, fans,
HVAC units, raised floors

5
00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:25.990
have worked for decades, but air can only
remove so much heat.

6
00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:30.535
With today's high-density racks,
processors run hotter and faster than

7
00:00:30.535 --> 00:00:30.990
ever.

8
00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:34.990
Cooling them with air alone pushes systems
to their limits.

9
00:00:34.990 --> 00:00:39.931
In fact, the U.S. Department of Energy
estimates that nearly 40% of a data

10
00:00:39.931 --> 00:00:40.990
center's energy use

11
00:00:40.990 --> 00:00:43.990
can go to cooling alone.

12
00:00:43.990 --> 00:00:48.990
That means higher operational costs,
greater environmental impact,

13
00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:51.990
and less energy available for actual
computing.

14
00:00:51.990 --> 00:00:54.990
The rise of artificial intelligence
accelerators,

15
00:00:54.990 --> 00:01:00.990
GPUs and high-performance processors has
intensified this challenge.

16
00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:04.990
These systems pack enormous power into
smaller spaces,

17
00:01:04.990 --> 00:01:09.990
creating thermal loads that air cooling
simply cannot manage efficiently.

18
00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:13.990
That's why the industry is turning to
liquid cooling.

19
00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:18.990
By moving beyond air, we can handle higher
densities, improve efficiency,

20
00:01:18.990 --> 00:01:23.990
and unlock the future of sustainable data
center design.

21
00:01:23.990 --> 00:01:26.990
In this course, we'll explore how.
